# Jolly Challenge — Frontend Overview

A frontend-only React challenge app. No backend — all state and logic run in the browser.
Source of truth: [docs/FRONTEND.mdc](../../docs/FRONTEND.mdc).
Architecture and requirements: [docs/DESIGN_DOC.md](../../docs/DESIGN_DOC.md).

## Purpose

- Deliver the Jolly frontend challenge in a clean, testable React codebase.
- Keep modules small and predictable so AI-assisted changes stay reviewable.
- Enforce quality gates (lint, typecheck, tests, spaghetti/security checkers) before merge.

## Stack

- **Runtime:** React 19 + TypeScript + Vite
- **Routing:** React Router
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS v4
- **Components:** shadcn/ui (do not recreate primitives — see DESIGN_DOC.md)
- **Server state:** TanStack Query (React Query)
- **Validation:** Zod
- **Tests:** Vitest + Testing Library

## Module layout

Feature code lives under `src/modules/<name>/` with `pages/`, `components/`, `hooks/`,
`schemas/`, `stores/`, `types/`, `routes.ts`, and `__tests__/`. Shared UI goes in
`src/common/`. Route wiring is centralized in `src/routes/index.tsx`.

